Independent architecture reviewer synthetic resource/history probe, 2026-10-04.
Source: docs/evidence/continuous-architecture-probe.rs
Toolchain: rustc 1.96.0 (ac68faa20 2026-05-25), x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu,
LLVM 22.1.2. Same Linux host as docs/VERIFICATION.md.

Commands, run from the repository root:
cargo build --offline --locked --release
rustc --edition=2024 -O /tmp/continuous-architecture-probe.rs --extern lumen_desktop=target/release/deps/liblumen_desktop-edcbcf0f5242ad41.rlib -L dependency=target/release/deps -o /tmp/continuous-architecture-probe
/tmp/continuous-architecture-probe

The probe source has been preserved in docs/evidence. The library hash identifies
the local release build configuration; Cargo replaced its contents after the
Uniform bulb-region fix. The probe was relinked for the post-fix measurement.
Outputs below preserve the reviewer's tool results; tab indentation is normalized.
RSS/HWM includes the complete probe process (including the preceding history
oracle), not only SamplingPlan. Sampling times use three iterations and exclude
screen capture, editor/native-window rendering, smoothing and physical/network
outputs. The resource workload is an intentionally extreme but valid synthetic
64-bulb, 2,048-zone, radius-1.0 layout. It is not a general performance claim.

Before the bulb-region optimization:
Reviewer history oracle: 10,000 operations passed; edits/undo/redo=[3327, 3292, 3381]
Reviewer synthetic stress: 64 bulbs / 2048 zones / radius 1.0; compile 122.84 ms; sample 30.06 ms/frame
VmHWM:    464192 kB
VmRSS:    464192 kB

After the bulb-region optimization:
Reviewer history oracle: 10,000 operations passed; edits/undo/redo=[3327, 3292, 3381]
Reviewer synthetic stress: 64 bulbs / 2048 zones / radius 1.0; compile 6.94 ms; sample 1.47 ms/frame
VmHWM:     18052 kB
VmRSS:     18052 kB

The independent deque oracle checks checkpoint/Undo/Redo equality, redo
invalidation, count-cap eviction, availability flags, retained-history byte
budget and resulting Config validity throughout its seeded operation sequence.
The stress probe checks returned light/zone cardinality and equality of every
zone within each sampled bulb. It does not exercise native platform adapters.

